Factory-to-Customer Shipping Route Efficiency Analysis

Business Research & Analytical Framework

1. Project Overview
Nassau Candy Distributor operates as a national distributor, delivering products from factories to customers across multiple regions in the United States.

Efficient logistics and transportation management are essential for maintaining customer satisfaction, controlling operational costs, and ensuring timely deliveries.

This project focuses on analyzing shipping and delivery data using Python to identify operational inefficiencies, understand delivery delays, evaluate transportation costs, and recommend improvements to logistics operations.

2. Business Problem

The company faces potential challenges in managing its shipping operations, including:

Delayed customer deliveries.

High transportation and shipping costs.

Inefficient shipping routes.

Regional differences in delivery performance.

Poor performance across certain shipping modes.

Reduced customer satisfaction due to late deliveries.
 Research Objectives

Evaluate overall shipping and delivery performance.

Identify regions with the highest delivery delays.

Analyze shipping costs across different shipping modes.

Identify products and orders associated with operational inefficiencies.

Examine the relationship between delivery delays and customer satisfaction.

Identify high-performing and low-performing shipping regions.

Develop actionable recommendations to optimize logistics operations.

